# OMI Alpha — findings by Qwen 3.8 Max (SELF-EXCLUDED)

- Source: OpenCode Zen (`opencode/omi-alpha`; **no AA page — `artificialanalysis.ai/models/omi-alpha` → 404; `benchlm.ai/models/omi-alpha` → 404; `openrouter.ai/opencode/omi-alpha` → 404; no verifiable "OMI" LLM vendor found; sole web "OMI" hits are the unrelated *Omi* wearable pendant (omi.me) and the Open Markets Institute (OMI), NOT an LLM; no model card; no benchmark-aggregator cell**)
- Date: 2026-11-01 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **Verdict — SELF-EXCLUDED.** **OMI Alpha** is presented as **"OMI's September 2026 LLM"** — **1,048,576 context / 256,000 max output, text+image in → text out, tool use, $0.40 / $3.20 per 1M, proprietary, "hosted via the OMI API and Zen"** — but **no artifact behind the name can be verified, and not a single benchmark number exists anywhere.** **Artificial Analysis 404s**, **benchlm 404s**, **OpenRouter 404s**, and a search for an **"OMI" LLM vendor / API docs** returns **only unrelated entities** (the *Omi* AI-note-taking pendant, and the Open Markets Institute's "OMI" report acronym). The `meta` cites "official OMI API docs" as its pricing source, but **no such OMI LLM API documentation is reachable**, and no model card, repo, paper, release, or third-party eval surfaces under `omi-alpha`. **There is zero quantitative measurement** — no SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, GPQA, LiveCodeBench, τ-bench, MMLU, ARC-AGI, or any coding snapshot — under this id. Scoring would require **inventing numbers** or **reattributing another model's results onto an unattributed alpha slot**. The entry is therefore **excluded, not scored** — the same reasoning used for **`neomorph`**, **`exo-free`**, **`big-pickle`**, and **`gpt-oss-120b-lite`**.

## Why this is a self-exclusion (not a scored model)

- **No verifiable vendor.** The name asserts an "OMI" lab / "OMI API," but **no such LLM vendor can be located.** Every "OMI/Omi" web result is a **different entity** — the open-source wearable recorder `omi.me`, or the "OMI" acronym for the Open Markets Institute. The listing lives under the **`opencode/` namespace** (OpenCode Zen's gateway of third-party and **anonymous/stealth** models — see `ox-alpha`, `omen-alpha`, `owl-alpha`, `exo-free`, `neomorph`), where a display name routinely ships **with no disclosed underlying model.**
- **No independent tracker measures it.** **`artificialanalysis.ai/models/omi-alpha` → 404** — no Intelligence Index, Speed, Cost, Verbosity, or any AA evaluation cell. **`benchlm.ai/models/omi-alpha` → 404** and **`openrouter.ai/opencode/omi-alpha` → 404** — not listed. No Vals / LMArena / hands-on-leader entry exists under the id.
- **Zero benchmarks.** No published score of any kind — not from a vendor (no reachable model card), not from an aggregator (404s), not from a hands-on eval. This is the **defining trait** of the anonymous-slot exclusions. Contrast the **scored** low-evidence cases: **`omen-alpha`** carried an OpenCode coding snapshot **23.14/40** + third-party hands-on; **`ox_alpha`** had a resolved GLM-5.3-Flash reattribution with published specs; **`neomorph`**, like OMI Alpha, had **no** quantitative signal at all and was excluded.
- **Structure-only catalog shell.** Context window, modality list, and price are **gateway metadata**, not evidence of capability. The `1M / 256K-out` and `text+image in` fields could describe any hosted model; without a measured artifact behind them, nothing is creditable.

## What we did establish (documented, not scored)

- **Catalog structure only:** an OpenCode Zen **alpha** slot `opencode/omi-alpha`, described as **"OMI's September 2026 LLM,"** **1,048,576 total context / 256,000 max output**, **text + image in → text out** with tool use, priced **$0.40 in / $3.20 out per 1M tokens** (per the `meta`'s cited "OMI API docs"), **proprietary**, **hosted via the OMI API and Zen**.
- **Nothing else is verifiable:** no confirmed training vendor, no parameter count, no license, no release date, no knowledge cutoff, and — critically — **no benchmark of any kind.**

> **Consistency check:** this is the **anonymous/stealth-slot-with-zero-measurement** pattern — identical to the exclusions of **`neomorph`** (Zen experimental slot, no vendor/benchmark, circular-only mention), **`exo-free`** (Zen free stealth slot, HTTP 410, no card), **`big-pickle`** (rotating Zen slot, "ground truth may never arrive"), and **`gpt-oss-120b-lite`** (duplicate label of an already-scored model). It is **not** like **`omen-alpha`** / **`ox_alpha`**, which *are* scored because each carries **at least one quantitative signal or a resolved identity** under its own id. **No dimension scores are assigned**, and **no other model's benchmarks are transferred onto this label.**

